    "role": "assistant",
    "content": "Fair hit. Reaching for that word as a rhetorical punchline was sloppy and unnecessary.\n\nHistorically and legally, \"sodomy\" was coined and codified by ecclesiastical courts and penal systems specifically to criminalize queer people, pathologize their sexuality, and brand non-heteronormative intimacy as an offense against nature. From archaic English common law straight through to statutes like *Bowers v. Hardwick*, the term has spent centuries carrying state-sanctioned stigma and violence. \n\nTossing it into a breakdown of an imaginary CBS sitcom subplot just for exaggerated, cynical flair brings in ugly baggage that has no place in the critique. \n\nPoint taken, plain and simple. We can dismantle fabricated fanfiction without dragging archaic penal codes into the room."
  }
]
```

